-- General Accounting Principles: Basic Accounting Concepts
('UPSC EPFO', 'General Accounting Principles', 'Basic Accounting Concepts', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'The fundamental accounting equation is expressed as:',
 '[{"text":"Assets = Liabilities + Capital","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Assets = Capital - Liabilities","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Liabilities = Assets + Capital","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Capital = Assets + Liabilities","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'The fundamental accounting equation states that a business''s total assets equal the sum of its liabilities and owner''s capital (equity).'),
('UPSC EPFO', 'General Accounting Principles', 'Basic Accounting Concepts', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'The accounting concept that treats a business as a separate entity from its owner is called the:',
 '[{"text":"Going concern concept","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Business entity concept","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Money measurement concept","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Matching concept","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'The business entity concept requires that a business''s financial transactions be recorded separately from the personal transactions of its owner(s).'),
('UPSC EPFO', 'General Accounting Principles', 'Basic Accounting Concepts', 'hard', 'mcq',
 'Under the accrual concept of accounting, revenue is recognized when it is:',
 '[{"text":"Earned, regardless of when cash is received","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Received in cash, regardless of when earned","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Budgeted for the year","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Approved by the auditor","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'The accrual concept requires revenue to be recognized when it is earned (goods delivered or services performed), not necessarily when cash is actually received.'),
('UPSC EPFO', 'General Accounting Principles', 'Basic Accounting Concepts', 'easy', 'mcq',
 'Which of the following is classified as a current asset?',
 '[{"text":"Cash in hand","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Land and building","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Long-term investments","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Plant and machinery","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Cash in hand is a current asset, since it is readily available and expected to be used within the normal operating cycle (typically one year).'),

-- General Accounting Principles: Financial Statements and Analysis
('UPSC EPFO', 'General Accounting Principles', 'Financial Statements and Analysis', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'The Balance Sheet of a business primarily shows:',
 '[{"text":"The financial position of the business at a particular point in time","isCorrect":true},{"text":"The profit or loss over a period","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Only the cash transactions of the business","isCorrect":false},{"text":"The tax liability for the year","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'A Balance Sheet is a snapshot of a business''s assets, liabilities, and capital as of a specific date, reflecting its financial position at that point in time.'),
('UPSC EPFO', 'General Accounting Principles', 'Financial Statements and Analysis', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'The Profit and Loss Account (Income Statement) of a business shows:',
 '[{"text":"The financial position at a point in time","isCorrect":false},{"text":"The net profit or loss over a period of time","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Only the fixed assets owned","isCorrect":false},{"text":"The share capital structure","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'The Profit and Loss Account reports a business''s revenues, expenses, and resulting net profit or loss accumulated over a specific accounting period.'),
('UPSC EPFO', 'General Accounting Principles', 'Financial Statements and Analysis', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'Depreciation is best described as:',
 '[{"text":"The systematic allocation of the cost of a fixed asset over its useful life","isCorrect":true},{"text":"An immediate cash outflow each year","isCorrect":false},{"text":"An increase in the market value of an asset","isCorrect":false},{"text":"A one-time write-off in the year of purchase","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Depreciation systematically spreads the cost of a fixed (tangible) asset over the periods it is expected to be used, matching the expense to the revenue it helps generate.'),
('UPSC EPFO', 'General Accounting Principles', 'Financial Statements and Analysis', 'hard', 'mcq',
 'The current ratio, a key measure of short-term liquidity, is calculated as:',
 '[{"text":"Current Assets / Current Liabilities","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Current Liabilities / Current Assets","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Total Assets / Total Liabilities","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Net Profit / Current Assets","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'The current ratio is calculated by dividing current assets by current liabilities, indicating a business''s ability to meet its short-term obligations.'),

-- Industrial Relations and Labour Laws: Industrial Relations
('UPSC EPFO', 'Industrial Relations and Labour Laws', 'Industrial Relations', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'The term "collective bargaining" refers to:',
 '[{"text":"An individual employee negotiating their own salary alone","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Negotiation between employers and a group of employees (or their union) over employment terms","isCorrect":true},{"text":"A government order fixing wages","isCorrect":false},{"text":"A court ruling on an industrial dispute","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Collective bargaining is the process by which employers and a group of employees (typically represented by a trade union) negotiate terms and conditions of employment.'),
('UPSC EPFO', 'Industrial Relations and Labour Laws', 'Industrial Relations', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'A "lockout" in the context of industrial relations refers to:',
 '[{"text":"Employees refusing to enter the workplace","isCorrect":false},{"text":"The closure of a workplace by an employer to prevent employees from working, typically during a dispute","isCorrect":true},{"text":"A government-ordered factory inspection","isCorrect":false},{"text":"A scheduled holiday for all employees","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'A lockout is initiated by the employer, temporarily closing a workplace or refusing to allow employees to work, typically as a response to an ongoing industrial dispute.'),
('UPSC EPFO', 'Industrial Relations and Labour Laws', 'Industrial Relations', 'hard', 'mcq',
 'Which official under the Industrial Disputes Act primarily handles industrial disputes through conciliation?',
 '[{"text":"Conciliation Officer","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Labour Court judge only","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Company auditor","isCorrect":false},{"text":"District Magistrate only","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'A Conciliation Officer, appointed under the Industrial Disputes Act, mediates between employers and employees to help resolve industrial disputes amicably.'),
('UPSC EPFO', 'Industrial Relations and Labour Laws', 'Industrial Relations', 'easy', 'mcq',
 'The term "strike" refers to:',
 '[{"text":"A temporary stoppage of work by employees as a form of protest","isCorrect":true},{"text":"An employer closing the factory permanently","isCorrect":false},{"text":"A government-mandated holiday","isCorrect":false},{"text":"A permanent resignation by all employees","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'A strike is a temporary, collective work stoppage undertaken by employees, typically to press demands or protest against employer actions.'),

